2. THE PATCH SERIES — BSD-3-Clause
-----------------------------------

core/patches/ is a series of patches against Chromium. Two kinds of content live
there and they carry the same terms for different reasons.

The context lines in every patch are Google's code, quoted so the patch can be
applied, and they remain under Chromium's BSD-3-Clause licence.

The lines Fury adds — including the files under components/fury/ that the series
creates outright — are licensed BSD-3-Clause by choice, not by obligation.
BSD-3-Clause imposes nothing on the licence of surrounding work, so these could
have been AGPL. They are not, so that a Chromium built from this series carries
one consistent set of terms and no copyleft obligation reaches somebody who only
wanted a browser.

The source files the series adds carry Chromium's own three-line header, which
refers to "the LICENSE file". Inside the Chromium checkout where that code
compiles, that resolves to core/src/LICENSE — Chromium's BSD-3-Clause text — and
not to the LICENSE file in this repository.


