licences of its many third-party dependencies. Nothing in this repository grants
any rights to that code.


5. WIDEVINE — NOT DISTRIBUTED, AND MUST NOT BE
-----------------------------------------------

The Widevine CDM is a proprietary binary licensed from Google. It is not in this
repository and cannot be redistributed without a licence.

core/args/macos-arm64-lowmem.gn builds with Widevine support enabled and
core/build/link-widevine.sh stages libwidevinecdm.dylib out of the Google Chrome
already installed on the build machine. That is lawful because the blob is
already licensed onto that machine and because it never leaves it.

The consequence is easy to overlook: a bundle built with those arguments
CONTAINS the blob, at
Chromium.app/Contents/Frameworks/Chromium Framework.framework/Versions/*/Libraries/WidevineCdm/.
Roughly 20 MB. Do not publish, upload or hand on such a build.

core/args/macos-arm64.gn sets enable_widevine = false and produces a bundle that
may be given to someone else. It also produces a browser that refuses
com.widevine.alpha where real Chrome accepts it, which is a three-line
detection. That is an open problem, recorded in the README and in
core/args/macos-arm64.gn, not a solved one.


6. REFERENCE CAPTURES
----------------------

tools/detect-suite/baselines/ holds three committed captures, all taken on
macOS arm64: real Chrome 150, an unpatched Chromium 150 build, and one Fury
profile running a Windows 11 persona through a proxy. They record what those
browsers report through their own web APIs. The third is the evidence for the
claims in the README — it is the capture the release gate passes 13 checks on.

They are redacted — the capturing machine's routable IP address, harvested from
WebRTC ICE candidates, is replaced with 203.0.113.7 from the RFC 5737
documentation range. Everything else is intentionally intact, because it is the
measurement: GPU model, screen geometry, installed fonts, audio latency, speech
voices, timezone. A capture describes the machine that took it. Anyone
publishing one should understand they are publishing a description of their own
computer.

Raw captures are not committed. See tools/detect-suite/baselines/.gitignore, and
`cargo run -p fury-detect -- redact --check` before committing one.
